Build the Our Works case study detail pages for the Boldteq marketing site. There are 9 portfolio items with detail pages.

**Project:** `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/Boldteq`
**Stack:** Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind 4, CSS Modules

**IMPORTANT:** Read CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md first. This project uses Next.js 16.2.3 — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for any breaking changes. Never use `any` type.

**Read first for patterns:**
- `src/lib/constants/pricing.ts` — constants pattern
- `src/app/page.tsx` — page composition
- `src/components/shared/cta-banner.tsx`

**Files to create:**

### 1. `src/types/portfolio.ts` — ADD to existing (if it exists, extend it; if not, create)
Add this interface:
```typescript
export interface PortfolioDetail {
  slug: string;
  platform: string;
  title: string;
  meta: { role: string; teamSize: string; duration: string };
  challenge: string;
  solution: string;
  implementation: string[];
  impact: { value: string; label: string; description: string }[];
  keyFeatures: string[];
  techStack: string[];
  gallery: string[];
}
```

### 2. `src/lib/constants/portfolio-details.ts`
9 case study detail entries. Here's the data extracted from the Webflow HTML detail pages:

```typescript
export const PORTFOLIO_DETAILS: PortfolioDetail[] = [
  {
    slug: "cinea",
    platform: "Shopify",
    title: "Premium Brand Shopify Redesign with Checkout Optimisation",
    meta: { role: "Lead Shopify Developer", teamSize: "3 Members", duration: "1 Month" },
    challenge: "Cinea's existing Shopify store looked outdated and failed to communicate the premium feel of their brand. A complete redesign was needed — without disrupting the live store.",
    solution: "We designed and developed a new custom Shopify theme with editorial-style layouts, dynamic product displays and a streamlined multi-step checkout. Every design decision was rooted in conversion data — reducing friction at each stage of the buyer journey.",
    implementation: [
      "Full custom Shopify theme build — editorial layouts, premium typography",
      "Dynamic product display with colour & variant switching",
      "Streamlined checkout flow — fewer steps, higher completion rate",
      "Brand identity cohesion across all pages and components"
    ],
    impact: [
      { value: "48%", label: "Add-to-Cart Rate", description: "Increase after redesign" },
      { value: "-34%", label: "Bounce Rate", description: "Homepage improvement" },
      { value: "+27%", label: "Checkout Completion", description: "Reduced drop-off" },
      { value: "4 weeks", label: "Delivery Time", description: "Full redesign & QA" }
    ],
    keyFeatures: [
      "Custom premium theme from scratch",
      "Dynamic product variant display",
      "Optimised multi-step checkout",
      "Full brand identity system"
    ],
    techStack: ["Shopify", "Liquid", "JavaScript", "CSS", "Figma"],
    gallery: [
      "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6936b27cc4d64679a58e166d/69aaae99f3e11e64fe731430_Home%20Client.png",
      "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6936b27cc4d64679a58e166d/69aab08fe64fc4b6ce7d0851_21.png",
      "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6936b27cc4d64679a58e166d/69aab00138b4184464328e7b_33.png"
    ]
  }
];
```

For the other 8 projects (betterdays, dabble, dog-crate, frames-for-prints, junoone, lippy-oil, repower-electric-supply, sandscents), read their HTML detail pages from `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/` to extract the same data structure. Each page follows the same pattern as cinea.

### 3. `src/components/our-works-detail/case-study-content.tsx` + `.module.css`
The main case study content component.
- Props: `{ detail: PortfolioDetail }`
- Layout: single column content sections

Sections (each with a colored icon indicator):
1. **The Challenge** (red accent) — heading + "Problem Statement" subtitle + paragraph
2. **Our Solution** (blue accent) — heading + "Strategic Approach" subtitle + paragraph
3. **Implementation** (purple accent) — heading + "Key Steps" subtitle + numbered list (01, 02, 03, 04)
4. **Impact & Results** (green accent) — heading + "Measurable Outcomes" subtitle + 2x2 grid of metric cards (value + label + description)
5. **Key Features** (orange accent) — heading + "Highlights" subtitle + checkmark list
6. **Tech Stack** — heading + row of tag pills

Icons from the Webflow export at:
- Challenge: `/images/webflow/Layer_1-62.svg`
- Solution: `/images/webflow/Layer_1-63.svg`
- Implementation: `/images/webflow/Layer_1-64.svg`
- Impact: `/images/webflow/Layer_1-65.svg`
- Key Features: `/images/webflow/Layer_1-66.svg`

Use `/images/webflow/Group-4.svg` for checkmark icons in key features.

### 4. `src/components/our-works-detail/case-study-gallery.tsx` + `.module.css`
Image gallery component:
- Props: `{ images: string[], title: string }`
- Simple gallery: show main image with thumbnail row below
- Uses `useState` to track selected image index
- Click thumbnail to switch main image
- Responsive, stacks to single column on mobile

### 5. `src/components/our-works-detail/case-study-hero.tsx` + `.module.css`
Hero section for detail page:
- Props: `{ detail: PortfolioDetail }`
- Badge: platform name (e.g., "Shopify")
- Title
- 3 meta items in a row: Role (with icon), Team Size (with icon), Duration (with icon)
- Use icons: `/images/webflow/Group-47135-2.svg` (role), `/images/webflow/Vector-27.svg` (team), `/images/webflow/Group-3.svg` (duration)

### 6. `src/app/our-works/[slug]/page.tsx`
Dynamic route. Server component.

```tsx
import { notFound } from "next/navigation";
import { PORTFOLIO_DETAILS } from "@/lib/constants/portfolio-details";
import { createMetadata } from "@/lib/seo/metadata";
import { CaseStudyHero } from "@/components/our-works-detail/case-study-hero";
import { CaseStudyContent } from "@/components/our-works-detail/case-study-content";
import { CaseStudyGallery } from "@/components/our-works-detail/case-study-gallery";
import { CtaBanner } from "@/components/shared/cta-banner";

// generateStaticParams for SSG
export function generateStaticParams() {
  return PORTFOLIO_DETAILS.map((d) => ({ slug: d.slug }));
}

// Dynamic metadata
export function generateMetadata({ params }: { params: { slug: string } }) {
  const detail = PORTFOLIO_DETAILS.find((d) => d.slug === params.slug);
  if (!detail) return {};
  return createMetadata({
    title: `${detail.title} | Case Study | Boldteq`,
    description: `${detail.challenge.slice(0, 155)}...`,
    path: `/our-works/${detail.slug}`,
  });
}

export default function CaseStudyPage({ params }: { params: { slug: string } }) {
  const detail = PORTFOLIO_DETAILS.find((d) => d.slug === params.slug);
  if (!detail) notFound();

  return (
    <>
      <CaseStudyHero detail={detail} />
      <div style={{ display: "grid", gridTemplateColumns: "1fr 1fr", gap: "40px", maxWidth: "1280px", margin: "0 auto", padding: "40px 5%" }}>
        <CaseStudyContent detail={detail} />
        <CaseStudyGallery images={detail.gallery} title={detail.title} />
      </div>
      <CtaBanner />
    </>
  );
}
```

NOTE: Check how Next.js 16 handles `params` in dynamic routes — it may be a Promise now. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for the correct pattern. Adapt accordingly.

**Important:** For the 2-column layout on the detail page (content left, gallery right), use CSS Modules instead of inline styles. The grid should stack to single column on mobile.

**Config:** The images use `cdn.prod.website-files.com` URLs. Make sure `next.config.ts` has this domain in `remotePatterns`. Another agent may add this — just verify it exists.

For the 8 remaining case studies, read each HTML file to extract the data. The files are at:
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/better-days.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/dabble.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/dog-crate.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/frames-for-prints.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/junoone.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/lippy-oil.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/repower-electric-supply.html`
- `boldteq-v1-0.webflow/our-works-pages/sandscents.html`

Each follows the same structure as cinea: platform badge, title, meta (role/team/duration), challenge, solution, implementation steps, impact metrics, key features, tech stack. Also extract the gallery image URLs from the CMS data CSV.

